**10:00 p.m.** and wakes up at **6:00 a.m.**\n- So, her **usual sleep duration** is:\n\n$$\n6:00 \\text{ a.m.} - 10:00 \\text{ p.m.} = 8 \\text{ hours} = 480 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Actual Sleep Time on This Day**\n\nWe are told she **woke up 5 minutes earlier than usual** (to go to the bathroom). So:\n\n- She woke up at **6:00 a.m. - 5 minutes = 5:55 a.m.**\n\nShe still **went to bed at 10:00 p.m.**, so normally she would have slept from **10:00 p.m. to 6:00 a.m.**, but she **woke up earlier**.\n\nThus, the **total time she was asleep** that day is:\n\n$$\n5:55 \\text{ a.m.} - 10:00 \\text{ p.m.}\n$$\n\nLet's compute that:\n\n- From **10:00 p.m. to 12:00 a.m.** is 2 hours = 120 minutes.\n- From **12:00 a.m. to 5:55 a.m.** is 5 hours 55 minutes = 355 minutes.\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n120 + 355 = 475 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Subtract Sleepwalking Time**\n\nWe are told that she **sleepwalked from 2:15 a.m. to 2:38 a.m.**  \nSo the time spent sleepwalking is:\n\n$$\n2:38 - 2:15 = 23 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\nThat time was **not** spent sleeping **on her bed** \u2014 it was time she was **sleepwalking** (i.e., awake but not in bed).\n\nSo, to find how long she **was asleep on her bed**, we subtract the 23 minutes of sleepwalking from her total sleep time:\n\n$$\n475 \\text{ minutes (total sleep time)} - 23 \\text{ minutes (sleepwalking)} = \\boxed{452} \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 **Final Answer:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{452} \\text{ minutes}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 14.846322536934169, "draft_calls": 0, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 139, "method": "native_ar", "output_hash": "11d48bb1296fb0bb919c093186cb8b9d8ac08f0963e8e2ab4ff90411c07cc413", "output_tokens": 566, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 20561936384, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 20891828224, "problem_id": "gsm8k/1695cf1a111991fc", "profile_regions_ms": {"unattributed_runtime": 14881.94990484044}, "rank": 0, "reference_answer": "452", "repetition": 0, "request_seconds":