{"acceptance_length": 6.157894736842105, "acceptance_lengths": [2, 2, 1, 13, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 1, 4, 9, 8, 4, 1, 2, 5, 3, 4, 15, 14, 16, 16, 8, 16, 13, 5, 6, 6, 16, 10, 4, 5, 9, 7, 1, 2, 3, 5, 2, 1, 2, 9, 13, 2, 2, 6, 5, 4, 6, 5, 16, 5, 3, 16, 2], "accepted_draft_lengths": [1, 1, 0, 12, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 5, 0, 3, 8, 7, 3, 0, 1, 4, 2, 3, 14, 13, 15, 15, 7, 15, 12, 4, 5, 5, 15, 9, 3, 4, 8, 6, 0, 1, 2, 4, 1, 0, 1, 8, 12, 1, 1, 5, 4, 3, 5, 4, 15, 4, 2, 15, 1], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 20455006208, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 20454988800, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "Let's break this problem down step by step.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Calculate total calories burned**\n\nHannah does two activities:\n\n1. **Aerobics:**  \n   - Time: 2 hours  \n   - Calories burned per hour: 500  \n   - Total calories burned from aerobics:  \n     $$\n     2 \\text{ hours} \\times 500 \\text{ calories/hour} = 1000 \\text{ calories}\n     $$\n\n2. **Running:**  \n   - Time: 1 hour  \n   - Calories burned per hour: 600  \n   - Total calories burned from running:  \n     $$\n     1 \\text{ hour} \\times 600 \\text{ calories/hour} = 600 \\text{ calories}\n     $$\n\n**Total calories burned:**  \n$$\n1000 + 600 = 1600 \\text{ calories}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Calculate the amount of water needed**\n\nHannah needs to drink **100 ml of water for every 200 calories** burned.\n\nFirst, find how many 200-calorie units are in 1600 calories:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1600}{200} = 8\n$$\n\nNow, multiply by the amount of water per 200 calories:\n\n$$\n8 \\times 100 \\text{ ml} = 800 \\text{ ml}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 **Final Answer:**\n$$\n\\boxed{800} \\text{ ml}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 2.2426378587260842, "draft_calls": 57, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 96, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "b4562dc664748ec2da6e0f1ccac13820bfd0fa9c413a7a3235ebec5f1d84b613", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "4d2f35c442fefbec83d008f35964629f681647bbe84428d0f16abca67ee267b4", "output_tokens": 351, "